1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,570
Startup investing means putting
money into a young private

2
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:07,017
company in exchange for a
security, such as shares or an

3
00:00:07,017 --> 00:00:09,788
agreement that may convert into
shares later.

4
00:00:09,788 --> 00:00:14,088
You are not buying a guaranteed
piece of a future success story.

5
00:00:14,088 --> 00:00:18,501
The company may grow, stay
small, change direction, or close,

6
00:00:18,501 --> 00:00:21,612
and your investment can lose all
its value.

7
00:00:21,612 --> 00:00:25,794
Unlike a public stock, a private
startup investment usually has no

8
00:00:25,794 --> 00:00:29,025
active market where you can sell
whenever you want.

9
00:00:29,025 --> 00:00:33,119
Before deciding, identify exactly
what security is offered, what

10
00:00:33,119 --> 00:00:37,341
rights it gives, how the business
plans to use the money, and what

11
00:00:37,341 --> 00:00:38,300
could go wrong.

12
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:42,450
Think of the money as money you
may not see again for a long time.

13
00:00:42,450 --> 00:00:46,850
A compelling founder or product
is only one part of the decision.

14
00:00:46,850 --> 00:00:50,443
Read the actual offering
documents, compare the price

15
00:00:50,443 --> 00:00:54,375
and terms, and decide whether
the risk fits your finances.

16
00:00:54,375 --> 00:00:57,985
Education is not a
recommendation to invest, and no

17
00:00:57,985 --> 00:01:00,888
platform can promise a startup’s
outcome.

